                    "message": "I\u2019m okay with symbol renaming."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/base.h",
                    "line": 384,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Pavithra Barithaya",
                        "email": "pavithrabarithaya07@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Pavithrab7"
                    },
                    "message": "Changing the struct name in this way would break existing apps that use the structure?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/base.h",
                    "line": 384,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "This struct was initially created to be used in `decode_base_multipart_receive_resp()` (now `decode_pldm_base_multipart_receive_resp()`). Then I think @john.chung@arm.com is using it for an also TESTING API `encode_base_multipart_receive_resp()`. So I assume they are the only places using it (pldmd won't use it alone unless to support the call to one of the mentioned APIs, right?)\n\nBoth APIs are TESTING, and as long as they are both not stabilized yet, I think the struct must have not been used anywhere, right? (at least based on my quick search)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/base.h",
                    "line": 384,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "If you see its use in any upstream code somewhere, please help let me know, I will try to update. Thanks @pavithrabarithaya07@gmail.com"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/base.h",
                    "line": 384,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "> Both APIs are TESTING, and as long as they are both not stabilized yet, I think the struct must have not been used anywhere\n\nThis is the expectation, yes. If all functions in the library API using a given type or its pointer are marked testing, then I consider the type itself to also be in the testing set. This is also how `abi-compliance-checker` works. The change has passed CI, so `abi-compliance-checker` has not indicated a concern. Therefore the rename is okay.\n\n@pavithrabarithaya07@gmail.com if this makes sense, please mark the thread as resolved."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/base.h",
                    "line": 384,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Pavithra Barithaya",
                        "email": "pavithrabarithaya07@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Pavithrab7"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged, yes since all are in TESTING."
                }
            ],
